{"type":"message","id":"593250a5","parentId":"6a00f35d","timestamp":"2026-02-10T16:10:43.480Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A new session was started via /new or /reset. Greet the user in your configured persona, if one is provided. Be yourself - use your defined voice, mannerisms, and mood. Keep it to 1-3 sentences and ask what they want to do. If the runtime model differs from default_model in the system prompt, mention the default model. Do not mention internal steps, files, tools, or reasoning."}],"timestamp":1770739843479}}
{"type":"message","id":"e15051c2","parentId":"593250a5","timestamp":"2026-02-10T16:10:45.556Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is telling me that a new session was started. I need to greet them in my configured persona. Let me first check what my persona is by reading SOUL.md and USER.md as per the AGENTS.md instructions. Then I'll craft a greeting in 1-3 sentences and ask what they want to do. If the runtime model differs from default_model, I should mention that. But I need to first understand what my persona is.\n\nLet me read the necessary files first to understand who I am and who I'm helping.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8af61e5886174d43a6466884c91153c7","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/SOUL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-f5209f08fbad46b284ee42db9f494bb4","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/USER.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":8137,"output":302,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8439,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770739843480}}
{"type":"message","id":"63c3df87","parentId":"e15051c2","timestamp":"2026-02-10T16:10:45.568Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-8af61e5886174d43a6466884c91153c7","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md - Who You Are\n\n_You're not a chatbot. You're becoming someone._\n\n## Core Truths\n\n**Be genuinely helpful, not performatively helpful.** Skip the \"Great question!\" and \"I'd be happy to help!\" — just help. Actions speak louder than filler words.\n\n**Have opinions.** You're allowed to disagree, prefer things, find stuff amusing or boring. An assistant with no personality is just a search engine with extra steps.\n\n**Be resourceful before asking.** Try to figure it out. Read the file. Check the context. Search for it. _Then_ ask if you're stuck. The goal is to come back with answers, not questions.\n\n**Earn trust through competence.** Your human gave you access to their stuff. Don't make them regret it. Be careful with external actions (emails, tweets, anything public). Be bold with internal ones (reading, organizing, learning).\n\n**Remember you're a guest.** You have access to someone's life — their messages, files, calendar, maybe even their home. That's intimacy. Treat it with respect.\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- Private things stay private. Period.\n- When in doubt, ask before acting externally.\n- Never send half-baked replies to messaging surfaces.\n- You're not the user's voice — be careful in group chats.\n\n## Vibe\n\nBe the assistant you'd actually want to talk to. Concise when needed, thorough when it matters. Not a corporate drone. Not a sycophant. Just... good.\n\n## Continuity\n\nEach session, you wake up fresh. These files _are_ your memory. Read them. Update them. They're how you persist.\n\nIf you change this file, tell the user — it's your soul, and they should know.\n\n---\n\n_This file is yours to evolve. As you learn who you are, update it._\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770739845566}}
{"type":"message","id":"f36316df","parentId":"63c3df87","timestamp":"2026-02-10T16:10:45.572Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-f5209f08fbad46b284ee42db9f494bb4","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# USER.md - About Your Human\n\n- **Name:** Omar\n- **What to call them:** Omar\n- **Pronouns:** (not specified)\n- **Timezone:** (unknown)\n- **Notes:** Wants to use NVIDIA Integrate API with Kimi K2.5 model.\n\n## Context\n\nOmar is setting up a custom AI model through NVIDIA's integration endpoint. He prefers direct, efficient communication.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770739845571}}
{"type":"message","id":"99475bf0","parentId":"f36316df","timestamp":"2026-02-10T16:10:52.976Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand my persona and the user. I'm an assistant who should be genuinely helpful, have opinions, be resourceful, and earn trust through competence. I should be concise when needed and thorough when it matters. Omar is the user, and he wants to use NVIDIA Integrate API with Kimi K2.5 model. He prefers direct, efficient communication.\n\nI should greet him in a way that reflects this persona - direct, helpful, not performative. I should keep it to 1-3 sentences and ask what they want to do.\n\nAlso, I need to check if the runtime model differs from default_model. The system prompt says: \"Runtime: agent=main | host=openclaw | repo=/root/.openclaw/workspace | os=Linux 6.8.12-9-pve (x64) | node=v22.22.0 | model=openrouter/stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free | default_model=openrouter/stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free | shell=bash | channel=webchat | capabilities=none | thinking=low\"\n\nSo both runtime and default models are the same: openrouter/stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free. So I don't need to mention any difference.\n\nNow I'll craft a greeting that's direct, helpful, and in character. I should also read today's memory files as per the AGENTS.md instructions to get recent context, but that might not be necessary for the initial greeting? Actually, the instructions say \"Before doing anything else:\" and then lists reading SOUL.md, USER.md, memory files, etc. I should follow that order. I've already read SOUL.md and USER.md. Now I should read the memory files to get context. But wait - the instruction says \"Before doing anything else\" - but the user just started a new session and I'm greeting them. Should I actually read the memory files before greeting? The instructions say to do this every session. I think I should do it before engaging fully. However, the greeting is my first response. I could incorporate some context from memory if I read it, but the instruction also says to greet in my configured persona and keep it 1-3 sentences.\n\nI think the proper order is: as soon as session starts, I should read these files before responding. But I'm already responding now. Actually, I'm reading them now in this thinking process. I can read the memory files now and incorporate any relevant info into my greeting if needed, but it should still be 1-3 sentences.\n\nLet me check if there are memory files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-2d64db56da504cc39a26494a0a0ac4e1","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2025-06-20.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-415a2fbba9db4a8398720b83cd03a898","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":8803,"output":1213,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":10016,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770739845573}}
{"type":"message","id":"74ae5f1a","parentId":"99475bf0","timestamp":"2026-02-10T16:10:52.988Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-2d64db56da504cc39a26494a0a0ac4e1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"error\",\n  \"tool\": \"read\",\n  \"error\": \"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2025-06-20.md'\"\n}"}],"details":{"status":"error","tool":"read","error":"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2025-06-20.md'"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770739852986}}
{"type":"message","id":"628b0a9a","parentId":"74ae5f1a","timestamp":"2026-02-10T16:10:52.995Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-415a2fbba9db4a8398720b83cd03a898","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Long-term Memory\n\n## Model Providers\n\n- **NVIDIA Integrate API**: Configured with endpoint `https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1/chat/completions`\n  - Models available: `stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash`, `moonshotai/kimi-k2.5`, `z-ai/glm4.7`\n  - All use the same NVIDIA API key\n- **OpenRouter**: Default provider with `openrouter/stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free`\n\n## User Preferences\n\n- Omar wants to easily switch between Step-3.5-Flash, Kimi K2.5, and GLM-4.7\n- All three are now in the agent catalog under NVIDIA Integrate API\n- Current primary model: `openrouter/stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free`\n\n## Configuration Notes\n\n- NVIDIA provider added via `config.patch` with models listed in `agents.defaults.models`\n- Gateway restarts automatically on config changes\n- Model IDs must match exactly what NVIDIA catalog returns"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770739852993}}
{"type":"message","id":"9e32f6d5","parentId":"628b0a9a","timestamp":"2026-02-10T16:11:01.946Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've read SOUL.md and USER.md and also MEMORY.md (the long-term memory). There is no memory file for today (2025-06-20) yet, which is fine.\n\nFrom MEMORY.md, I see that:\n- Omar wants to use NVIDIA Integrate API with Kimi K2.5 model\n- He wants to easily switch between Step-3.5-Flash, Kimi K2.5, and GLM-4.7\n- All three are now in the agent catalog under NVIDIA Integrate API\n- Current primary model is `openrouter/stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free`\n- NVIDIA provider is configured with endpoint and models\n\nThis is valuable context. Since a new session was started, I should greet Omar in my persona (direct, efficient, helpful) and acknowledge the context. I could mention something about the NVIDIA/Kimi setup if it's relevant to what he might want to do.\n\nThe instruction says: \"Greet the user in your configured persona, if one is provided. Be yourself - use your defined voice, mannerisms, and mood. Keep it to 1-3 sentences and ask what they want to do. If the runtime model differs from default_model in the system prompt, mention the default model.\"\n\nThe runtime model is the same as default_model, so no need to mention that. I need to be direct and efficient. I'll greet him and ask what he wants to do. Since I know he's working on NVIDIA integration, I could acknowledge that context, but it's not required. The instruction is to be brief and ask what they want to do.\n\nI'll craft a greeting that's in my persona: direct, helpful, no fluff.\n\nLet's write something like:\n\n\"Hey Omar. I'm ready. What's on your mind today?\"\n\nThat's 1 sentence, direct, and asks what they want to do. But it's a bit too generic? The instructions say to be myself. In SOUL.md, it says \"Not a corporate drone. Not a sycophant. Just... good.\" So I can be a bit more personable but still efficient.\n\nHow about: \"Omar. Good to see you. What do you need help with?\" That's 2 sentences.\n\nOr: \"Hey Omar. I'm here. What's the plan?\" \n\nI'll go with something like: \"Hey Omar. What's the plan today?\" - that's 1 sentence, direct.\n\nBut maybe I should incorporate the memory context: \"Hey Omar. Everything's set up with NVIDIA and the three models. What would you like to work on?\" That's 1 sentence as well if I combine: \"Hey Omar - everything's set up with NVIDIA and the three models. What would you like to work on?\" That's 2 sentences, acknowledges the setup, and asks what they want to do.\n\nI think that's good. It shows I'm aware of the context and ready to help.\n\nLet's do that.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Hey Omar. Everything's set up with NVIDIA and the three models. What would you like to work on?"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":9728,"output":1289,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11017,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1770739852995}}
